      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1068",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Scientific name:</strong> Pterobunocephalus depressus (Haseman, 1911)</li><li><strong>Common name:</strong> Banjo Catfish</li><li><strong>Type locality:</strong> Río Machupo near San Joaquín, Amazon system, Bolivia.</li><li><strong>Synonyms:</strong> Buncephalus depressus, Bunocephalus albofasciatus</li><li><strong>Size:</strong> 89 mm (3.5\") SL.</li><li><strong>Identification:</strong> Smaller than Bunocephalus species and can most readily be distinguished from that genus by the number of anal fin rays (11-20 in Pterobunocephalus vs. 5-10 in Bunocephalus).</li></ul>"
    },
    {
